"output_config.effort": "high", "thinking.display": "summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": ["Agent", "Bash", "Edit", "Read", "Skill", "TaskStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 1864, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 1864, "cached_input": 36443, "input": 38309, "output": 152}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 33044, "other": 423, "system": 34815, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 28134}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 110813}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "29318d58-2caf-5d99-9d9a-0455934e66f3", "at": 1795624404.2311444, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 15586, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "eca6de07218ffdacb8887242ec7a1fbf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "d20c8459-5522-5d1f-9d1e-cc14cae4d0d7", "at": 1795624404.2409027, "until": 1795624405.5214489, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 15587, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "eca6de07218ffdacb8887242ec7a1fbf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01UoFVpfw3t6djit5Z7gGJ8W", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian && cp srw/Outline.md /tmp/Outline_r2.md; rm -rf srw && git clone -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" srw && cd srw && git log --oneline | head -4 && git diff HEAD~1 HEAD", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian && cp srw/Outline.md /tmp/Outline_r2.md; rm -rf srw && git clone -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" srw && cd srw && git log --oneline | head -4 && git diff HEAD~1 HEAD"]], "output": "```console\nc2b55f8 Outline rev 3: nine-page NeurIPS budget (5 figures, 3 tables in text), Brief rev 4 rules for k*, transform and small-N panels\n4f9f6d4 Outline rev 2: two-predictor k*, history sweep, transform as method, small-N LLM panels, owners for reproduction notes\n53aa467 Outline: story, claims, experiments and figures for the paper\ndiff --git a/Outline.md b/Outline.md\nindex 2625a61..cb91dd9 100644\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n # Outline: which k benchmarks to run, and how well do they predict the rest?\n \n-(Outline revision 2, after the review in `story-repo`#3; revision 1 was the first draft. Built from the `Brief` of idea-repo, revision 3 (2026-11-25 16:08 UTC). It says what to test, not what a result must be. Thresholds, definitions and hypotheses H1-H4 are the Brief's and are not restated in full; where this page names one, the Brief governs.)\n+(Outline revision 3: fits NeurIPS 2026 Main Track's nine pages (`story-repo`#4) and Brief revision 4 (`idea-repo`#5); revision 2 followed the review in `story-repo`#3. Built from the `Brief` of idea-repo, revision 3 (2026-11-25 16:08 UTC). It says what to test, not what a result must be. Thresholds, definitions and hypotheses H1-H4 are the Brief's and are not restated in full; where this page names one, the Brief governs.)\n \n ## 1. The story in one paragraph\n Evaluating a new model on N benchmarks is costly; leaderboards hold a history matrix of M models x N benchmarks. An evaluator can run only k benchmarks and wants the other N-k scores. Prior work shrinks the items *inside* one benchmark, or shows that benchmark scores are low-dimensional, but does not treat \"which k to run\" as a design problem, give a k-versus-error law, or test the answer where it matters: for a new family or a newer, stronger model. We (i) set up a leakage-free, family-clustered, paired protocol for this question; (ii) give a closed-form k-curve for a linear-Gaussian latent-factor model and check it in three tiers; (iii) compare greedy Bayesian A-optimal selection with random and standard selectors under a fixed predictor grid; and (iv) report honestly how much of the answer survives family/time shift and in which data regimes. The method is a known toolkit (PPCA/EM + Gaussian conditioning + greedy A-optimal); the contribution is the protocol, the finding, and the verified theory, in that order.\n@@ -23,15 +23,15 @@ Each claim lists the evidence needed (for `experiment-repo`) and what the main f\n | # | Claim (a question, not a result) | Evidence needed | Carrying figure/table |\n |---|---|---|---|\n | C0 | The data regimes are what the paper says they are: dense-pool size, density, how pool models differ from the rest, family structure, spectrum/r_eff, time-proxy validity. | Data audit per dataset: counts, density, PCA/participation ratio, r_eff by held-out likelihood, near-duplicate share, MTEB first-commit bulk test; **dense-pool selection check** (how pool models differ from the rest in size, release time, mean score), so the reader knows what a dense-pool result is a claim about; number of families per dataset. | Table 1 (datasets and regime) + Fig. A1 (spectra). |\n-| C1 | **k-curve and k\\*** (H1): how fast does error fall with k, how large must k be for closure 0.9/0.8/0.95, and is the knee near r_eff? | Greedy and random selection, grouped K-fold, k = 1..min(10, N/2); C(k) against LOBO reference (primary) and in-sample reference (optimistic); k\\* with censoring; H1 outcome per dataset. **k\\* belongs to selector and predictor together, so it is reported for two predictors: PPCA, and the best simple predictor (one-factor offset, ridge/PLS) chosen on the training folds only, never on test folds; the paper's answer to \"how large must k be\" is the smaller of the two, with both shown.** Also run on the small-N LLM cross-benchmark matrices (HELM Lite 91 x 10, Open LLM Leaderboard 6; k <= N/2, labelled small-N case studies, not evidence for how large k). | **Fig. 2 (main result)**: stand\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "c26d5b26-dd60-5a62-9b6a-952b394e115b", "at": 1795624405.103574, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 15656, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "eca6de07218ffdacb8887242ec7a1fbf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "17aea0b1-36bd-5705-b423-a3abd571043b", "at": 1795624405.1103497, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 15657, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "eca6de07218ffdacb8887242ec7a1fbf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "5de3d872-e7aa-5f0a-a28b-9de1d28bd94f", "at": 1795624405.1148877, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 15658, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "eca6de07218ffdacb8887242ec7a1fbf", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "d8c055a3-0405-533b-92b7-fca21799fa5b", "at": 1795624405.1848402, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 15663, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "eca6de07218ffdacb8887242ec7a1fbf", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challenge → credential-required", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "credential challenge 